Enhancement: lock parity Phase 2 append transaction boundary

Backup, merge, and copy destination writes now use a restricted append-only
repository transaction capability. It permits blob/tree/pack/index uploads and
snapshot saves but does not expose any remove API, making accidental deletion
from these workflows a compile-time error. `key add` now correctly uses the
exclusive lock policy because its key validation may remove a broken new key.

Concurrent `backup` + `backup` + `merge` and `backup` + `copy` destination
integration tests pass under `-race`, followed by `check`. Append writers keep
their non-exclusive lock while classic prune has no deletion revalidation; they
are not yet feature-driven lock-free.

